{"availability":"available","full":"fmiras/potterscript","name":"potterscript","description":"The Wizarding World Programming Language written in Rust","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":38,"forks":2,"created":"2023-08-04T21:31:35Z","updated":"2023-09-16T20:38:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://potterscript.fmiras.com","topics":["esoteric-language","harry-potter","hogwarts","language","nom","parser","rust","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://potterscript.fmiras.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.860Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.860Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.860Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.860Z","stars":38,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Parody Programming Language based in Harry Potter (Wizarding World). Experience the magical world of coding like never before! It's a really useful to project to learn Rust and how programming languages are done.","Ever wished you could speak the magical language of wizards and witches? PotterScript is your enchanted gateway to code with the charm and mystery of the Wizarding World.","This project is a remarkable endeavor to understand the magical connection between human logic and machine interpretation. It's a journey filled with trials, failures, and the sweet taste of success that only comes from the relentless pursuit of something extraordinary."],"features":["In PotterScript there are no such things as functions or args, but there are spells and targets. To cast a spell you have to use the wand character followed by the spell name and the target expression.","You can only cast a spell on one target, and the spell will do something with the target. For example, the Revelio {target} spell will print the target expression (variable or raw value) to the console.","Spells can also of course mutate the target, like Engorgio {target} that will increment the target value by one.","Aguamenti (no target): Returns \"💦\"","AvadaKedabra (no target): Process exit (Rust's panic!())"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fmiras/potterscript/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"522368e5dc03362be5530ed70369bf500997ad80177152a0f960d2704e77bf1b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.971Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.971Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Parody Programming Language based in Harry Potter (Wizarding World). Experience the magical world of coding like never before! It's a really useful to project to learn Rust and how programming languages are done.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fmiras/potterscript/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"522368e5dc03362be5530ed70369bf500997ad80177152a0f960d2704e77bf1b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fmiras/potterscript/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.971Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-09-16T20:38:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fmiras/potterscript/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:47.972Z","hash":"522368e5dc03362be5530ed70369bf500997ad80177152a0f960d2704e77bf1b","originalBytes":5174,"storedBytes":5174,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["target","string","runtime","potterscript","snake","some","spell","index","parser","revelio","value","like","magical","potter","variable","console","engorgio","example","language","number","programming","project","quidditch","rust","spells","wasm","world","cast","code","hat","loops","one","playground","prints","returns","running","sorting","values","wingardiumleviosa","wizarding","background","because","binary","black","code.","compiler","expression","features","flags","functions","house","incendio","journey","memory","only","periculum","possible","printing","program","repl","ron","serpensortia","snitch","something","statements","there","transforms","white","adapted","affiliated","after","aguamenti","any","